# Bytes are bytes (18_windows_port program decision 9): the core never
# normalizes line endings, fixtures may be deliberately CRLF or mixed,
# and byte-stability tests compare working-tree files verbatim. Disable
# git's eol conversion for every path so a checkout is byte-identical
# on every platform regardless of the machine's core.autocrlf. Without
# this, autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) smudges fixtures to
# CRLF and the canvas byte-stability suite fails on Windows.
* -text

# The Windows C# sources carry a few DELIBERATE CRLF terminators inside
# otherwise-LF files, and two tools disagree about them: `dotnet format`
# re-emits the trivia it touches using the platform newline and fails the
# verify gate if those lines are LF, while `git diff --check` reports the
# CR as trailing whitespace. Four review round-trips were spent on that
# disagreement before it was named. This tells git the CRs are
# deliberate; it changes no bytes, so `* -text` above still governs
# checkout and the canvas byte-stability fixtures are untouched.
#
# The alternative considered and rejected: normalize these files to
# all-CRLF, which satisfies both tools but rewrites every line of every
# file and buries real diffs under an EOL flip.
apps/slate-windows/**/*.cs whitespace=cr-at-eol

demo-vault/.obsidian/themes/** binary
demo-vault/attachments/*.mp3 binary
demo-vault/attachments/*.pdf binary
demo-vault/attachments/*.png binary
